  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>EDM activeXTextClass</name>
    <text>This BSA data is read out slowly and is intended to capture
snapshots of a single transmission from LLRF to BSA. 
If PID Before equals PID After, then it is a synchronous data set.
(That PID is the lower 32 bits of the global timing PID.)

Synchronous data sets are stored in these PVs:

$(CM)00:PRCA:BSADIAG_DATA
$(CM)00:PRCB:BSADIAG_DATA

They are 10-element arrays with these contents:

If you prefer to use scalars and/or do not require
synchronous sets, you can also use the PVs below.</text>
    <x>24</x>
    <y>76</y>
    <width>352</width>
    <height>236</height>
    <font>
      <font family="Liberation Sans" style="REGULAR" size="12.0">
      </font>
    </font>
    <foreground_color>
      <color name="black-14" red="0" green="0" blue="0">
      </color>
    </foreground_color>
    <background_color>
      <color name="GLOBAL canvas" red="200" green="200" blue="200">
      </color>
    </background_color>
    <vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment>
  </widget>
